{"title":"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(ingenious)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (ingenious)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(cool)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (cool)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_AM-GM\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 AM-GM</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Alcumus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Alcumus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(If_You_Don&#39;t_Know_Vieta)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (If You Don't Know Vieta)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e036578f2792e66924f453935efc734ab1b042e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 - 18x^3 + kx^2 + 200x - 1984 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"277\" height=\"16\" />, the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of its roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/5/445213f58312143e7cb2f3679f18e526e33dc6c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$- 32$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28ingenious.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(ingenious)\">Solution 1 (ingenious)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (ingenious)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using Vieta's formulas, we have: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/8/a086ae1a74f1ad0803016044a93bdab65fd48d11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}a+b+c+d &amp;= 18,\\\\ ab+ac+ad+bc+bd+cd &amp;= k,\\\\ abc+abd+acd+bcd &amp;=-200,\\\\ abcd &amp;=-1984.\\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"292\" height=\"87\" /> \n</p><p><br /> \nFrom the last of these equations, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/8702f5d5ba2ce857b5d3b5dcfc26dfd92311e73c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cd = \\frac{abcd}{ab} = \\frac{-1984}{-32} = 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"201\" height=\"37\" />. Thus, the second equation becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/9/a193fdda84e2727c72cfedad58ca9a6a6a68f057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-32+ac+ad+bc+bd+62=k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"267\" height=\"16\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/802363709cb6f728f0649b5ce16cdd06cc036c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ac+ad+bc+bd=k-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"210\" height=\"14\" />. The key insight is now to factor the left-hand side as a product of two binomials: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/5/235044cdcef26052f270e6535a2ac08d6b3a92aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(c+d)=k-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"181\" height=\"18\" />, so that we now only need to determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add2609af1bb7632cc22b68fd49fdd94de06b327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/5/dd54f8129186e28453c8c19f0c38ca25420a8e9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"14\" /> rather than all four of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/6/bb60e0857a2c0a2c47acfbe81781032feb1f7150.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c,d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badf81798ae6974db42441bc8b1974e4af74b70c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=a+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"74\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b498aae5e0d7e6e4dcfae05605b15c7b0c2b0edc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=c+d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />. Plugging our known values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/e/f6e1a0789128066a6b03855158dafabb8d84f63b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cd$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> into the third Vieta equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/49220c2a92d76304ae73dd5d94946764f22baf37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-200 = abc+abd + acd + bcd = ab(c+d) + cd(a+b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e2fce1b748a72b04f592e11deea344d8f4efa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-200 = -32(c+d) + 62(a+b) = 62p-32q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"346\" height=\"18\" />. Moreover, the first Vieta equation, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9a822c14b80a3b4c0d17cefcc951d7d0ea62b28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c+d=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"143\" height=\"14\" />, gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9feb320dbe8fa7aa1c69838decdd49b7715e812f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />. Thus we have two linear equations in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, which we solve to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a357c84c81d686a8626309f21556457c55a7bac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23da437ccd712252114166265b4a597ca6e46624.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/3/7630fdafd28677ea2357cf5f2b9b44e86a160dcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\underbrace{a+b}_4)(\\underbrace{c+d}_{14}) = k-30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"181\" height=\"37\" />, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/3/4136a4a1b5d8b7d6b34efd1091becbabef4d0989.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=4\\cdot 14+30 = \\boxed{86}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"169\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28cool.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(cool)\">Solution 2 (cool)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (cool)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We start as before: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76e96479b712673ab7b737fa40b8d710e96da1a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab=-32$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20a1af0c6b81f27701d04c2be22380d69b3a611f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$cd=62$\" width=\"59\" height=\"12\" />. We now observe that a and b must be the roots of a quadratic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/e/09ecf87dfe13d4002b98b76c41c90eb989f190cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+rx-32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"99\" height=\"16\" />, where r is a constant (secretly, r is just -(a+b)=-p from Solution #1). Similarly, c and d must be the roots of a quadratic <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d1314d0f24c7a2e4c3b1583c9877c6fc3bfe858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+sx+62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />. \n</p><p>Now \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f62175aaa7f80e68251443233a58c60988723717.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}x^4-18x^3+kx^2+200x-1984 =&amp; (x^2+rx-32)(x^2+sx+62)\\\\  =&amp; x^4+(r+s)x^3+(62-32+rs)x^2\\\\ &amp;+(62s-32r)x-1984.\\end{align*}\" width=\"525\" height=\"72\" />\n</p><p>Equating the coefficients of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/48524d3889ec8433cb03669176e738011df245b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> with their known values, we are left with essentially the same linear equations as in Solution #1, which we solve in the same way. Then we compute the coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76b2878564ab19b80abb21ba964abe90fe120846.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2$\" width=\"16\" height=\"15\" /> and get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412590af1938a0f486e4e2e0e697032168e39b67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=\\boxed{86}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"67\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_AM-GM\">Solution 3 AM-GM</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 AM-GM\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e871a5edfc4edb9e5a841a5f072e9ea9066de399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2, r_3, r_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"11\" /> be the roots of the polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/3/e036578f2792e66924f453935efc734ab1b042e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^4 - 18x^3 + kx^2 + 200x - 1984 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"277\" height=\"16\" />. We are given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac1215356c87eac6f3102e867b95e4dcc2d4a32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 r_2 = -32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>By Vieta's formulas, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dc06cc58142e551da9a65043a165648ee9402b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1+r_2+r_3+r_4 = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"174\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6fe79beca073b04b4751c76ed7f6473d5971d14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2+r_1r_3+r_1r_4+r_2r_3+r_2r_4+r_3r_4 = k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"335\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cf22572ef5631467015765faf26f2ed3fede5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2r_3+r_1r_2r_4+r_1r_3r_4+r_2r_3r_4 = -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"322\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f297f21fa3985959894c66269a12c8e179ae1876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2r_3r_4 = -1984$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552847ce627e6c5a8b5f1e0bedae41b55b954fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2 = -32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/5/bb5f9a34f18ee53fa8a4a18847e3029c515c6057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-32)r_3r_4 = -1984$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea3dcff11c90908c916b8ecbd937af14c127acd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3r_4 = \\frac{-1984}{-32} = 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"154\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/c/31cf22572ef5631467015765faf26f2ed3fede5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2r_3+r_1r_2r_4+r_1r_3r_4+r_2r_3r_4 = -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"322\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c0186509d7c6b50bc4910f7a0252d5fa9ee91be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2(r_3+r_4)+r_3r_4(r_1+r_2) = -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"288\" height=\"20\" />. Substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552847ce627e6c5a8b5f1e0bedae41b55b954fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2 = -32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e01a0a1047ab0cf9167d613071f1bc6c75a8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3r_4 = 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a256b8317435411b5bdb8eac83e7da10122446a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-32(r_3+r_4)+62(r_1+r_2) = -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"276\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67b246bdb7df9347526911075895652143901f27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = r_1+r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c44064b21f9bac4dcf3fffc0c8796b118c5f80e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = r_3+r_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/8/708c1f763c94e8d1432e140cbb2b51b4a8ba26b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A+B = 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/9/8292b3770b8c25957b0c0303cc765292033f57b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 18-A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />. Substituting this into the equation, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eeffeb30d286355b2f46f01481af0a786eb34ee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-32B+62A = -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"169\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/9/69971c5f9c3dea606ed56141debd9a34f336badf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-32(18-A)+62A = -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"20\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/7/bd744739947ab3abff71c17a41aec62d9ca00345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-576+32A+62A = -200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"217\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2cf86785e53d8b5ba8970ef18a1f5c32dbb4503.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$94A = 376$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/4/ad457bf51aee2cecb4638dc2a49f61960e7fd8e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\frac{376}{94} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9e4adf2f3c7827a708d8ba3c3f554eb03236553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B = 18-A = 18-4 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"211\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>So we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d8c20971e4a66fc72127663cdc56bf98ba3bbc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1+r_2 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"89\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/552847ce627e6c5a8b5f1e0bedae41b55b954fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1r_2 = -32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"15\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c5d1bf74c4c9ce00c8adbc73aba655e61f6413a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-4x-32 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/8/d88756011ab8b7ccc2acf0658e511e9984002c26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x-8)(x+4) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/57189720280f8ae630654ed176b4eb9df1a83488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a2fa73c0741add0e1865a94d03061a9c00f445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2 = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"17\" /> (or vice versa).\n</p><p>Also we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/9/f49e532f0a5ca03c1c23141b4992c58c27baaa96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3+r_4 = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/e/d0e01a0a1047ab0cf9167d613071f1bc6c75a8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3r_4 = 62$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"17\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae5f496b8ddda88b5cbbc06ccb02bee0580fd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7ce82c4f62f7e439d80be7f44293f527af4619b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/1/0d1838612e2f6c09aac967279877efbb87966cc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2-14x+62 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" />. Using the quadratic formula, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d4596c358cd50f3ef367be6d0ce44b5e19b63aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\frac{14 \\pm \\sqrt{14^2-4(62)}}{2} = \\frac{14 \\pm \\sqrt{196-248}}{2} = \\frac{14 \\pm \\sqrt{-52}}{2} = 7 \\pm i\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"560\" height=\"43\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/d/a6db873180f601737909c82ee60d97eac6f81654.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3 = 7+i\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36baeceb4ca8cd9eb64945cdf0a696952686541a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_4 = 7-i\\sqrt{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>We want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/2/af27256d2755f83aca7f48370196fa9cf7a2f8bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = r_1r_2+r_1r_3+r_1r_4+r_2r_3+r_2r_4+r_3r_4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"335\" height=\"17\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/0/c5065d455045d7083b8e4c22c1d396cb73ee2d2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = r_1r_2+r_3r_4 + (r_1+r_2)(r_3+r_4) = -32+62+(4)(14) = 30+56 = 86$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"578\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Final Answer: The final answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/60912368ea74a74e9a92f740a0404e362c16486a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{86}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~avm2023\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Alcumus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Alcumus)\">Solution 4 (Alcumus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Alcumus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since two of the roots have product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2e3cbc3294946500990cd24ce72375e8bda8c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-32,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"39\" height=\"17\" /> the equation can be factored in the form\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/1/6c1f3705bd38f556dd8f8383b0f7c91640bc9f31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^4 - 18x^3 + kx^2 + 200x - 1984 = (x^2 + ax - 32)(x^2 + bx + c).\\]\" width=\"489\" height=\"20\" />Expanding, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/1/b519c2117b6113dca04e49b2d390d997e7d3e3d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^4 - 18x^3 + kx^2 + 200x - 1984 = x^4 + (a + b) x^3 + (ab + c - 32) x^2 + (ac - 32b) x - 32c = 0.\\]\" width=\"622\" height=\"20\" />Matching coefficients, we get\n\\begin{align*}\na + b &amp;= -18, \\\\\nab + c - 32 &amp;= k, \\\\\nac - 32b &amp;= 200, \\\\\n-32c &amp;= -1984.\n\\end{align*}Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/9/fb999a0f5edfe992329e4b7673af309c8dddfad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c = \\frac{-1984}{-32} = 62,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"136\" height=\"40\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/4/b54bbdc3e49612f258ef9343e7ae28d78331090c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62a - 32b = 200.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"134\" height=\"16\" /> With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/63966318edfa68c3e66d0b096ce235c0b4f6db6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = -18,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" /> we can solve to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/7/4776d545e58865e347c9c5d3991937c1cc143d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = -4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/2/6722c67f87e8a4d113c00830bcab2b2e45c80c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = -14.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"16\" /> Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8dad62649633b3451f0979e2d88850ebfedbdc00.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = ab + c - 32 = \\boxed{86}.\\]\" width=\"179\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28If_You_Don.27t_Know_Vieta.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(If_You_Don't_Know_Vieta)\">Solution 5 (If You Don't Know Vieta)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (If You Don&#39;t Know Vieta)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that any given quartic polynomial can be factored into two quadratic polynomials. We see that for any given quadratic, the product of it's roots is:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/4/10467ad3090b4ad193ca50fc8badfa101830992f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{-b - \\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\cdot \\frac{-b + \\sqrt{b^{2}-4ac}}{2a} = \\frac{b^{2}-b^{2}+4ac}{4a^{2}} = \\frac{c}{a}\\]\" width=\"432\" height=\"40\" />\nWe see that both quadratics must have leading coefficient of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/d/48d02444a59b917b64e8bd0963b88712fc7fa0a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>We first try a quadratic where the product of it's roots is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b27e78a52924deeb2b1c266b916211ead13d32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-32$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd111f84d604782c041b000c8faa63c9ec9fe8af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{2}+b_{1}x-32\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\nWe then see that the other quadratic has the form\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/a/d1ad301599f0c5e8cebf312edac54e6db55ded4d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{2}+b_{2}x+62\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" />\nsince the constant term in both quadratics must multiply to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/3/01309a1b70e7bb52fbd475e870b2942b5b44c747.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1984$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>To get our general form quartic from these, we multiply\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/a/5ea1aae759b14d0fa11f7d8e18b229c217d3ef48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x^{2}+b_{1}x-32)(x^{2}+b_{2}x+62)\\]\" width=\"237\" height=\"20\" />\nExpanding, then combining coefficients, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690748e5b2cd71db91c8bfdeffc4f084fa6cd38e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{4}+b_{2}x^{3}+62x^{2}+b_{1}x^{3}+b_{1}b_{2}x^{2}+62b_{1}x-32x^{2}-32b_{2}x-1984\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b883bf5a27cda49d0eb09f49b69795fc33ee4f4f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{4}+(b_{1}+b_{2})x^{3}+(30+b_{1}b_{2})x^{2}+(62b_{1}-32b_{2})x-1984\\]\" width=\"443\" height=\"20\" />\nLooking back at our original polynomial, we extract the system\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f454c8c4c07afc2bd3d638c21d7fe9d810940ac1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{cases} b_{1}+b_{2} = -18 \\\\ 62b_{1}-32b_{2} =200 \\\\ 30+b_{1}b_{2} = k \\end{cases}\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"74\" />\nTo solve it, we see\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/a/40a863d568e7d0a47c1d19179566d5679d1fee9d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_{1} =-b_{2}-18\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/214b08983615d757b2134888da9eb13804c0fc25.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[62(-b_{2}-18)-32b_{2} =200\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/0/ec09af32191b78d411b3e81868b0cc84df879efa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[31(-b_{2}-18)-16b_{2} =100\\]\" width=\"208\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/a/20ab38bd52b7d7637153e60d2d9ccdfcd1e499f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-47b_{2} =658\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d77ce07cb098abafd899f99f413a05577794f309.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_{2} = -14\\]\" width=\"71\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/376f92a60abe169623ff8d42278d55e9ef68f2c5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b_{1} = -4\\]\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3a5f1ea309d98096a950a40d00803f94ca363e8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k = 30 + 56\\]\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/0/4d072ab555202e5479cf6b8aa6042a25d095d268.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{k=86}\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"24\" />\n~shockfront99\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Omega_Learn\">Video Solution by Omega Learn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Omega Learn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Dp-pw6NNKRo?t=316\">https://youtu.be/Dp-pw6NNKRo?t=316</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO\" title=\"1984 USAMO\">1984 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1984\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First<br />Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1984 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017174716\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.053 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.072 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 589/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1240/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 54/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 20068/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.958      1 -total\n 55.34%    6.618      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.19%    5.045      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:8330:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017174716 and revision id 281668. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}